    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0509" n="1967" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p2/pg1967"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320.2–AC/4–1951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            United States Mission at the United Nations
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-04-19T17:00:00-05:00">April 19, 1951—5
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>863. Dept commends ur efforts in AMC Subctee and
                    suggests you continue to press for AMC
                    recommendation to GA along lines position paper
                    Apr 12. Pls broaden consultations to include those members of AMC not represented on Subctee submitting US points
                    in form which wld make it possible for them to obtain authorization from their
                    Govts to proceed. FYI Dept now preparing
                    approaches to UK, Fr and Australia with view to obtaining early AMC action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
